problem:
(Total 50 points) Let $x_{1}, x_{2}, \cdots, x_{n}$ and $a_{1}, a_{2}, \cdots, a_{n}$ be two sets of real numbers satisfying the following conditions:
(1) $\sum_{i=1}^{n} x_{i}=0$;
(2) $\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left|x_{i}\right|=1$;
(3) $a_{1} \geqslant a_{2} \geqslant \cdots \geqslant a_{n}\left(a_{1}>a_{n}, n \geqslant 2\right)$.
Find the range of values for $m$ such that the inequality $\left| \sum_{i=1}^{n} a_{i} x_{i} \right| \leqslant m\left(a_{1}-a_{n}\right)$ always holds.
